usb: complete the EP0 control transfer when stalling it

usbd_ep_set_stall() only set USB_CX_STL for EP0. After the stack stalls an
OUT control request (with or without a data stage), the controller ignores
every following control transfer until the next bus reset; IN requests are
not affected. Setting USB_CX_DONE after USB_CX_STL lets the next SETUP be
handled. Measured on BL616CL with CherryUSB CDC ACM (Linux host, usbfs):
without this change EP0 stops after the first stalled vendor OUT request;
with it 50 of 50 rounds recover.

Applies to drivers/lhal/src/bflb_usb_v2.c of bouffalo_sdk v2.3.37
(identical to lhal master 911501a).
Upstream review: https://gerrit.bouffalolab.com/c/bouffalo/drivers/lhal/+/11805
Drop this patch when sources.json moves to an SDK release that contains it.

--- a/drivers/lhal/src/bflb_usb_v2.c
+++ b/drivers/lhal/src/bflb_usb_v2.c
@@ -1198,6 +1198,13 @@
         regval = getreg32(BFLB_USB_BASE + USB_DEV_CXCFE_OFFSET);
         regval |= USB_CX_STL;
         putreg32(regval, BFLB_USB_BASE + USB_DEV_CXCFE_OFFSET);
+
+        /* Also complete the control transfer. Otherwise, after an OUT request
+         * is stalled, the controller ignores every following control transfer
+         * until the next bus reset. */
+        regval = getreg32(BFLB_USB_BASE + USB_DEV_CXCFE_OFFSET);
+        regval |= USB_CX_DONE;
+        putreg32(regval, BFLB_USB_BASE + USB_DEV_CXCFE_OFFSET);
     } else {
         if (USB_EP_DIR_IS_OUT(ep)) {
             regval = getreg32(BFLB_USB_BASE + USB_DEV_OUTMPS1_OFFSET + (ep_idx - 1) * 4);
